# Repo material no build step reads. Keeping it out of the upload makes
# deploys smaller and means the design files and the SQL are not sitting on a
# web host.
#
# EVERY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and must stay that way.
# These are gitignore patterns: a bare `supabase/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, which silently excludes `lib/supabase/` — the Supabase
# clients the whole app imports — and the build fails with "Module not found"
# on a file that is right there in the repo.

# 33 design HTML files. Source of truth for the UI, read by humans, never
# imported by the app.
/design_elements/

# Migrations, seeds and the pgTAP suite. Applied with the Supabase CLI from a
# developer machine or CI, never from a Vercel build.
/supabase/

# Specs, architecture notes, the handoff.
/docs/

# Agent and editor config.
/.claude/
/AGENTS.md

/.github/
